1
00:00:24,241 --> 00:00:26,241
Thitinant Inganan!

2
00:00:26,242 --> 00:00:28,242
Stop making all that annoying noise!

3
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:31,920
And another thing,could you dress
more appropriately for the workplace?

4
00:00:32,278 --> 00:00:34,278
So you judge people
by what they wear, Boss?

5
00:00:34,675 --> 00:00:36,675
I've never thought I'm above anyone.

6
00:00:36,676 --> 00:00:38,787
But I've never lowered
my standards,either.

7
00:00:38,787 --> 00:00:39,621
Ow!

8
00:00:39,621 --> 00:00:40,787
Then how about a bet?

9
00:00:40,788 --> 00:00:41,954
One day,

10
00:00:41,954 --> 00:00:43,954
those high standards of yours

11
00:00:43,955 --> 00:00:47,012
will come down for this girl.

12
00:00:47,427 --> 00:00:49,427
You'll end up begging to
get into bed with me.

13
00:01:12,577 --> 00:01:13,377
Never mind

14
00:01:15,744 --> 00:01:17,544
Give it to me. I’ve got it.

15
00:01:20,011 --> 00:01:20,811
Careful.

16
00:01:49,177 --> 00:01:51,344
Hey, Boss, you can drop me off here.

17
00:01:55,344 --> 00:01:56,604
You live here?

18
00:01:57,546 --> 00:02:01,441
Look kind of shady.

19
00:02:05,411 --> 00:02:06,408
You don't trust people here...

20
00:02:08,234 --> 00:02:10,242
Or you don't trust me?

21
00:02:11,911 --> 00:02:13,148
You.

22
00:02:15,150 --> 00:02:16,319
But...

23
00:02:17,909 --> 00:02:20,171
It really doesn't look like
a nice place to live.

24
00:02:28,144 --> 00:02:31,077
I guess your idea of a decent place
to live is different from mine, Boss.

25
00:02:33,411 --> 00:02:35,011
I can walk to my room myself.

26
00:02:35,477 --> 00:02:36,711
You can leave me here, Boss.

27
00:02:37,011 --> 00:02:37,811
Thank you.

28
00:02:40,011 --> 00:02:40,911
Don't act tough.

29
00:02:41,344 --> 00:02:42,677
I'll walk you to your room.

30
00:02:51,144 --> 00:02:52,344
Are you sure about that, Boss?

31
00:02:53,744 --> 00:02:55,744
My room's on the third floor.

32
00:02:56,777 --> 00:02:57,877
And there's no elevator.

33
00:03:00,577 --> 00:03:02,711
How are you supposed to get
there alone in your condition?

34
00:03:03,544 --> 00:03:05,277
Are you going to hold the handrail
as you go up?

35
00:03:14,877 --> 00:03:15,677
Fine.

36
00:03:17,177 --> 00:03:19,744
But you have to hold on
to me tight, okay?

37
00:03:22,544 --> 00:03:23,344
Okay.

38
00:03:33,144 --> 00:03:36,250
Hey, what perfume are you wearing?

39
00:03:37,428 --> 00:03:38,665
It smells nice.

40
00:03:41,197 --> 00:03:42,493
What perfume do I use, huh?

41
00:03:46,077 --> 00:03:47,377
I'm not wearing any perfume.

42
00:03:52,111 --> 00:03:53,344
You like this scent, Boss?

43
00:03:57,177 --> 00:03:58,144
It does smell nice.

44
00:03:58,944 --> 00:04:00,344
It smells clean, like baby powder.

45
00:04:01,744 --> 00:04:06,077
But I just fell into a pool
of stagnant water.

46
00:04:08,077 --> 00:04:08,877
Ew!

47
00:04:09,311 --> 00:04:10,877
How do you like this scent, Boss?

48
00:04:17,611 --> 00:04:18,411
Ow!

49
00:04:18,877 --> 00:04:20,111
Just go.

50
00:04:32,944 --> 00:04:33,744
Hey!

51
00:04:34,477 --> 00:04:36,011
Why do you have to get
your face so close to mine?

52
00:04:36,611 --> 00:04:37,411
You're annoying.

53
00:04:38,577 --> 00:04:40,944
So you can catch
my scent clearly, Boss.

54
00:04:44,677 --> 00:04:46,295
Move your head away.

55
00:04:46,707 --> 00:04:49,777
And hurry up and walk, keep walking.
You're so heavy!

56
00:04:50,744 --> 00:04:52,012
Stop yapping.

57
00:04:52,895 --> 00:04:55,811
You're the one who said
you'd take responsibility for my life.

58
00:04:59,257 --> 00:05:00,544
yeah, yeah.

59
00:05:00,544 --> 00:05:02,507
Hurry... Just keep moving.

60
00:06:50,144 --> 00:06:51,218
Your room...

61
00:06:51,630 --> 00:06:53,311
It's actually nicer than I expected.

62
00:06:55,011 --> 00:06:58,577
Why? Did you think I'd be sleeping
in a pile of garbage, Boss?

63
00:06:59,711 --> 00:07:01,544
Uh... Nothing.

64
00:07:08,077 --> 00:07:08,877
What?

65
00:07:08,977 --> 00:07:09,777
Nothing.

66
00:07:11,277 --> 00:07:12,311
Want me to take your
jacket off for you?

67
00:07:14,977 --> 00:07:15,777
Come here.

68
00:07:40,177 --> 00:07:40,977
Come here.

69
00:07:41,144 --> 00:07:42,144
I'll take your shoes off for you.

70
00:07:44,744 --> 00:07:45,611
You're so sweet.

71
00:07:51,344 --> 00:07:52,877
I'll do it myself.

72
00:07:58,211 --> 00:08:01,077
Oh, you can do it yourself after all.

73
00:08:05,911 --> 00:08:08,377
Are you always this nice
to everyone, Boss?

74
00:08:10,977 --> 00:08:12,542
I'm never nice to anyone.

75
00:08:13,131 --> 00:08:15,820
And I'm especially mean to
people who treat me badly.

76
00:08:15,820 --> 00:08:18,219
Including you.

77
00:08:19,711 --> 00:08:21,144
And this is you being mean?

78
00:08:23,011 --> 00:08:25,311
I wonder how nice you'd be
if you were being nice.

79
00:08:27,041 --> 00:08:30,313
That person is going to be so lucky.

80
00:08:34,711 --> 00:08:35,511
Uh...

81
00:08:36,144 --> 00:08:38,931
Well, if that's everything, I'll...

82
00:08:39,343 --> 00:08:40,215
get going.

83
00:08:41,077 --> 00:08:41,877
Ow!

84
00:08:42,677 --> 00:08:43,477
Ow!

85
00:08:45,344 --> 00:08:46,144
It's hurt.

86
00:08:46,677 --> 00:08:49,013
Ow, it hurts. It hurts.

87
00:08:49,411 --> 00:08:50,211
Let me see.

88
00:08:51,144 --> 00:08:52,077
Where else does it hurt?

89
00:08:52,711 --> 00:08:55,319
Right here.

90
00:09:02,477 --> 00:09:03,277
Why are you smiling?

91
00:09:05,311 --> 00:09:06,111
What?

92
00:09:06,977 --> 00:09:08,211
I'm not smiling.

93
00:09:09,611 --> 00:09:10,411
It hurts.

94
00:09:11,177 --> 00:09:12,944
So I'm just gritting my teeth.

95
00:09:17,077 --> 00:09:18,411
Stop being so dramatic.

96
00:09:21,511 --> 00:09:22,311
Ow.

97
00:09:24,477 --> 00:09:26,177
Ow, that hurts.

98
00:09:30,544 --> 00:09:31,377
What are you doing?

99
00:09:33,511 --> 00:09:36,288
Nothing. I was just sneaking a peek.

100
00:09:36,641 --> 00:09:38,930
To see if you secretly disgust me?

101
00:09:41,477 --> 00:09:44,511
If I did, would I have gone
this far for you?

102
00:09:54,477 --> 00:09:55,529
Do you have any ice?

103
00:09:56,883 --> 00:09:59,611
I'll ice it for you so
you'll finally stop complaining.

104
00:10:00,311 --> 00:10:02,977
I do, but it's okay.
I can get it myself.

105
00:10:03,677 --> 00:10:05,818
Just sit still, will you?

106
00:10:06,583 --> 00:10:07,992
I'll get it.

107
00:10:08,522 --> 00:10:11,211
In your state, just sit down.
It is over there, right?

108
00:10:12,211 --> 00:10:13,177
In the fridge.

109
00:10:14,911 --> 00:10:15,711
Okay.

110
00:10:29,344 --> 00:10:31,611
Ow! That's cold.

111
00:10:32,577 --> 00:10:36,111
Hang in there.
It'll keep the swelling down.

112
00:10:48,277 --> 00:10:51,144
Do you live by yourself?

113
00:10:53,711 --> 00:10:57,344
Yes, My parents passed away
when I was little.

114
00:11:01,111 --> 00:11:03,511
Uh, sorry for asking.

115
00:11:05,177 --> 00:11:06,011
It's okay.

116
00:11:09,711 --> 00:11:10,511
Eh?

117
00:11:10,811 --> 00:11:11,611
What?

118
00:11:12,677 --> 00:11:13,877
Why do you ask, Boss?

119
00:11:16,311 --> 00:11:19,277
Or are you starting to fall for me?

120
00:11:21,977 --> 00:11:23,511
I was just making polite conversation.

121
00:11:24,544 --> 00:11:25,344
Oh, really?

122
00:11:25,911 --> 00:11:26,711
Mm-hmm.

123
00:11:27,544 --> 00:11:28,977
You drove me home...

124
00:11:30,177 --> 00:11:31,111
Carried me up to my room...

125
00:11:32,744 --> 00:11:34,377
And even put ice on my injury.

126
00:11:35,211 --> 00:11:36,877
If you're not interested, then fine.

127
00:11:37,977 --> 00:11:39,211
I was just asking.

128
00:11:42,677 --> 00:11:44,377
But thank you, Boss.

129
00:11:47,777 --> 00:11:50,306
Uh, what I did...

130
00:11:51,130 --> 00:11:52,329
Was because I was the one who hurt you.

131
00:11:53,448 --> 00:11:54,771
Don't read too much into it.

132
00:11:59,277 --> 00:12:00,811
I'm not reading anything into it.

133
00:12:02,277 --> 00:12:03,744
You're awfully defensive, Boss.

134
00:12:06,944 --> 00:12:08,077
Or are you afraid...

135
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:13,011
That I'll find out
you've got a soft spot for me?

136
00:12:24,544 --> 00:12:25,911
Here. Ice it yourself.

137
00:12:27,144 --> 00:12:28,311
I'm going home.

138
00:12:30,577 --> 00:12:31,777
Wait, Boss.

139
00:12:33,177 --> 00:12:34,811
Can you stay with me for a while?

140
00:12:36,577 --> 00:12:37,377
Please?

141
00:12:38,077 --> 00:12:39,577
Stay with me a little longer.

142
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:43,461
Please?

143
00:12:45,711 --> 00:12:46,511
Oh.

144
00:12:47,611 --> 00:12:48,411
The power's out.

145
00:13:03,077 --> 00:13:03,877
Is that normal?

146
00:13:07,477 --> 00:13:08,277
Hey.

147
00:13:09,677 --> 00:13:10,611
What are you looking for?

148
00:13:10,877 --> 00:13:11,911
A flashlight.

149
00:13:16,377 --> 00:13:18,677
Hey, wait! Where are you going?

150
00:13:19,677 --> 00:13:20,777
To get a candle.

151
00:13:21,144 --> 00:13:21,872
A candle?

152
00:13:22,166 --> 00:13:22,886
It's fine.

153
00:13:23,652 --> 00:13:25,544
I'll get it. You stay here.

154
00:13:26,611 --> 00:13:27,411
Where is it?

155
00:13:29,511 --> 00:13:33,111
Uh, there's a candle up there.

156
00:13:34,111 --> 00:13:36,377
Okay. Stay put.

157
00:14:17,877 --> 00:14:19,177
How romantic.

158
00:14:24,577 --> 00:14:26,077
There's nothing romantic about this.

159
00:14:27,944 --> 00:14:30,344
Doesn't this place have
a backup generator?

160
00:14:31,344 --> 00:14:32,144
Ow!

161
00:14:32,211 --> 00:14:34,477
How could a cheap rental like this

162
00:14:35,011 --> 00:14:36,777
have a backup generator, Boss?

163
00:14:37,477 --> 00:14:39,511
It loses power as soon as
it rains a little.

164
00:14:44,144 --> 00:14:47,577
But the power will be back soon.
Just give it a minute.

165
00:14:52,911 --> 00:14:55,811
It's not like I plan to stay here
with you until the power comes back.

166
00:14:56,777 --> 00:14:57,944
I've had a long day.

167
00:14:58,744 --> 00:14:59,544
I want to rest.

168
00:15:12,544 --> 00:15:14,111
Want to rest here, Boss?

169
00:15:16,177 --> 00:15:18,177
I'll be your pillow.

170
00:15:24,111 --> 00:15:24,795
No, thanks.

171
00:15:25,266 --> 00:15:26,569
You're practically bone-dry.

172
00:15:26,922 --> 00:15:29,162
Going back to sleep at my condo

173
00:15:29,162 --> 00:15:31,423
would be way more peaceful.

174
00:15:56,677 --> 00:15:59,144
Boss...

175
00:16:02,977 --> 00:16:04,452
So...

176
00:16:07,632 --> 00:16:09,334
Aren't you ever scared
living in a place like this?

177
00:16:12,801 --> 00:16:13,682
Nope.

178
00:16:15,010 --> 00:16:16,303
What are you afraid of, Boss?

179
00:16:17,744 --> 00:16:18,760
Running out of money.

180
00:16:20,998 --> 00:16:22,277
I'm afraid of that too.

181
00:16:23,944 --> 00:16:24,744
Oh!

182
00:16:25,211 --> 00:16:26,911
But now I've got something else
to be afraid of.

183
00:16:28,311 --> 00:16:29,111
I'm afraid...

184
00:16:29,744 --> 00:16:31,411
Of weirdos like you...

185
00:16:31,711 --> 00:16:32,511
Coming into my life.

186
00:16:33,011 --> 00:16:33,811
Too late.

187
00:16:34,977 --> 00:16:36,577
Because a weirdo like me...

188
00:16:37,811 --> 00:16:40,511
Has already wormed
my way into your life.

189
00:16:44,144 --> 00:16:45,677
What are you, a parasite?

190
00:16:48,544 --> 00:16:49,411
That's harsh, isn't it?

191
00:16:53,277 --> 00:16:55,240
I could be even harsher.

192
00:16:56,064 --> 00:16:59,611
So you'd better be a good little
servant and do as I say.

193
00:17:06,011 --> 00:17:07,744
When Boss drops the tough act...

194
00:17:09,511 --> 00:17:11,311
You're actually pretty cute.

195
00:17:17,211 --> 00:17:18,011
Watch it!

196
00:17:27,277 --> 00:17:28,077
Boss...

197
00:17:29,411 --> 00:17:30,211
Hmm?

198
00:17:30,811 --> 00:17:33,711
Stay with me until
the power comes back.

199
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:37,843
Please?

200
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:39,961
Please?

201
00:17:39,961 --> 00:17:41,843
Keep me company, okay?

202
00:17:42,468 --> 00:17:43,317
Mmm...

203
00:17:44,377 --> 00:17:45,177
Fine.

204
00:17:59,612 --> 00:18:00,552
Boss...

205
00:18:00,552 --> 00:18:01,551
Hmm?

206
00:18:04,344 --> 00:18:06,577
Have you started falling for me yet?

207
00:18:17,544 --> 00:18:18,344
Not yet.

208
00:18:45,777 --> 00:18:47,577
Ow! Wh-What...?

209
00:18:48,777 --> 00:18:50,011
Why are you getting up, Boss?

210
00:18:52,744 --> 00:18:53,611
I'm fine.

211
00:18:54,711 --> 00:18:55,577
I'm going home.

212
00:18:56,711 --> 00:18:57,511
And...

213
00:18:57,677 --> 00:18:59,077
If you still can't walk tomorrow...

214
00:18:59,111 --> 00:19:00,911
Don't bother showing up at the office.

215
00:19:01,144 --> 00:19:01,944
I'm sick of it.

216
00:19:03,411 --> 00:19:04,877
Come pick me up tomorrow too, Boss.

217
00:19:05,311 --> 00:19:06,111
No.

218
00:19:06,577 --> 00:19:09,977
But you said you'd
take responsibility for my life.

219
00:19:11,677 --> 00:19:13,311
You have to come pick me up
tomorrow, Boss.

220
00:19:13,811 --> 00:19:15,677
Because if you don't come pick me up...

221
00:19:15,877 --> 00:19:17,344
I'll report you to
the Department of Labour.

222
00:19:17,577 --> 00:19:19,277
For running over your own employee.

223
00:19:19,477 --> 00:19:20,277
How about that?

224
00:19:20,611 --> 00:19:21,411
Scared yet?

225
00:19:23,911 --> 00:19:25,011
You're such a little brat.

226
00:19:26,111 --> 00:19:27,077
Thitinant!

227
00:19:28,177 --> 00:19:29,711
Keep dreaming. I'm not coming!

228
00:19:36,321 --> 00:19:37,614
Bye-bye.

229
00:20:04,111 --> 00:20:04,911
Damn it!

230
00:20:06,477 --> 00:20:08,277
Why is my heart beating so fast?

231
00:20:23,344 --> 00:20:24,477
What's wrong with her?

232
00:20:25,477 --> 00:20:27,911
She was fine when the power went out.

233
00:20:48,677 --> 00:20:49,511
That crazy brat.

234
00:20:53,311 --> 00:20:54,811
What am I even doing here?

235
00:21:05,144 --> 00:21:07,544
Don't forget to delete Yong's video.

236
00:21:25,744 --> 00:21:27,229
You want me to delete it, Boss?

237
00:21:27,229 --> 00:21:28,674
In your dreams!

238
00:21:29,911 --> 00:21:34,277
I went to so much trouble
to get that video.

239
00:21:36,377 --> 00:21:39,853
I've had enough, Ms. Chat!

240
00:21:41,090 --> 00:21:43,067
Please, just let me go.

241
00:21:44,304 --> 00:21:45,805
Please, just let me go.

242
00:21:46,777 --> 00:21:47,970
Oh, Yong!

243
00:21:48,618 --> 00:21:50,497
Make your face look sadder!

244
00:21:51,145 --> 00:21:52,454
Ms. Chat is smart, you know.

245
00:21:52,807 --> 00:21:55,377
If she finds out we're faking this...

246
00:21:55,777 --> 00:21:57,522
Ow, you idiot!

247
00:21:57,816 --> 00:21:59,611
This is pathetic enough already!

248
00:22:01,911 --> 00:22:03,544
I've bowed to the camera
four times now!

249
00:22:03,677 --> 00:22:05,811
Keep bowing like this.
Ugh, my back hurts!

250
00:22:06,311 --> 00:22:07,111
Hang in there.

251
00:22:07,611 --> 00:22:09,477
Because if she finds out
we're faking it...

252
00:22:09,811 --> 00:22:12,811
We're both as good as dead.

253
00:22:13,711 --> 00:22:14,511
Rin.

254
00:22:14,811 --> 00:22:16,377
Add some blood to
the corner of his mouth.

255
00:22:16,811 --> 00:22:17,611
Come here.

256
00:22:17,711 --> 00:22:18,777
Turn your face this way.

257
00:22:20,372 --> 00:22:21,489
Stay still.

258
00:22:24,944 --> 00:22:26,511
That's enough. Come sit here.

259
00:22:28,277 --> 00:22:29,077
Three.

260
00:22:29,111 --> 00:22:29,911
Two.

261
00:22:30,277 --> 00:22:31,077
One.

262
00:22:31,811 --> 00:22:34,620
I've had enough, Ms. Chat!

263
00:22:35,183 --> 00:22:36,334
I've had enough!

264
00:22:41,311 --> 00:22:42,575
If you want me to delete it...

265
00:22:44,401 --> 00:22:46,883
Come to my room and delete it yourself.

266
00:22:58,944 --> 00:22:59,944
This is Boss's jacket...

267
00:23:22,111 --> 00:23:23,811
I left my suit jacket
at that brat's place.

268
00:23:49,612 --> 00:23:50,905
Boss, you left your jacket here.

269
00:23:50,905 --> 00:23:52,375
Your jacket smells so good.

270
00:23:52,375 --> 00:23:55,489
I'm borrowing it to sleep in tonight.

271
00:23:58,877 --> 00:24:01,677
How dare you call me baby?

272
00:24:12,253 --> 00:24:15,714
I'm wearing this to work tomorrow.

273
00:24:16,284 --> 00:24:17,073
Huh?

274
00:24:26,377 --> 00:24:27,177
Damn it!

275
00:24:27,877 --> 00:24:28,677
Theerachat.

276
00:24:29,177 --> 00:24:30,344
Get a hold of yourself.

277
00:25:04,877 --> 00:25:06,677
If Boss sees this whole set...

278
00:25:08,111 --> 00:25:08,911
She's definitely got flustered.

279
00:25:11,744 --> 00:25:12,944
See you tomorrow, Boss.

280
00:25:40,577 --> 00:25:42,211
She's really good at getting
under my skin.

281
00:25:45,077 --> 00:25:46,011
Boss Chat.

282
00:25:46,744 --> 00:25:47,544
Yes?

283
00:25:47,677 --> 00:25:50,677
Ms. Sopha would like to discuss
this year's budget ahead of schedule.

284
00:25:51,544 --> 00:25:52,344
Hmm.

285
00:25:52,611 --> 00:25:53,347
Sure.

286
00:25:53,347 --> 00:25:53,877
All right.

287
00:25:54,377 --> 00:25:57,411
I'll coordinate the details for you.

288
00:25:58,211 --> 00:25:59,017
That should be...

289
00:25:59,017 --> 00:25:59,777
Good Morning.

290
00:26:01,744 --> 00:26:02,544
Good Morning.

291
00:26:04,677 --> 00:26:05,477
Wait a minute.

292
00:26:05,944 --> 00:26:07,711
She's really wearing that to work?

293
00:26:10,211 --> 00:26:11,011
You've got to be kidding me.

294
00:26:15,077 --> 00:26:16,117
This is bad, Secretary Han.

295
00:26:16,117 --> 00:26:16,977
Yes?

296
00:26:17,144 --> 00:26:18,711
Go distract Ms. Sopha.

297
00:26:18,811 --> 00:26:20,711
Talk about stocks,
the weather, anything!

298
00:26:21,077 --> 00:26:21,711
Go, now!

299
00:26:21,711 --> 00:26:22,111
Uh...

300
00:26:22,111 --> 00:26:22,646
Right now!

301
00:26:22,646 --> 00:26:23,336
Understood, Boss.

302
00:26:23,336 --> 00:26:23,836
Go, go!

303
00:26:24,177 --> 00:26:25,777
Ms. Sopha.

304
00:26:25,944 --> 00:26:26,277
Um...

305
00:26:26,277 --> 00:26:28,577
Regarding this year's annual budget...

306
00:26:28,944 --> 00:26:29,744
At this point...

307
00:26:29,877 --> 00:26:31,744
I think we may need to
make some adjustments.

308
00:26:38,311 --> 00:26:39,711
Do you want to get fired?

309
00:26:44,977 --> 00:26:46,177
What the hell are you doing?

310
00:26:47,611 --> 00:26:49,777
I couldn't breathe, Boss.

311
00:26:53,711 --> 00:26:55,477
And why are you dressed
like this at work?

312
00:26:57,977 --> 00:26:59,677
You gave me permission last night.

313
00:27:02,211 --> 00:27:03,020
Besides...

314
00:27:03,550 --> 00:27:05,878
If I wear your suit jacket like this...

315
00:27:06,290 --> 00:27:08,885
Everyone will know I'm already taken.

316
00:27:12,577 --> 00:27:15,277
That's ridiculous. Take it off. Now.

317
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:22,360
So, you want me to take this off?

318
00:27:22,882 --> 00:27:23,913
Yeah.

319
00:27:24,524 --> 00:27:25,320
Okay.

320
00:27:32,411 --> 00:27:33,446
Stop!

321
00:27:34,859 --> 00:27:35,811
Don't take it off.

322
00:27:41,911 --> 00:27:43,597
First you tell me to take it off,
then to put it on.

323
00:27:43,891 --> 00:27:45,077
What do you want?

324
00:27:48,177 --> 00:27:51,077
Leave it on.
Wear it over your outfit like that.

325
00:27:52,611 --> 00:27:53,511
Why?

326
00:27:54,377 --> 00:27:56,577
Because what
you're wearing underneath is...

327
00:28:02,577 --> 00:28:03,877
It's hideous.

328
00:28:04,544 --> 00:28:05,966
Absolutely hideous.

329
00:28:08,111 --> 00:28:08,911
Hideous?

330
00:28:09,377 --> 00:28:10,177
Yeah.

331
00:28:10,477 --> 00:28:11,777
And don't let me catch you...

332
00:28:11,977 --> 00:28:13,611
Taking off that jacket
before the end of the workday.

333
00:28:14,311 --> 00:28:16,111
Or I'll deduct it from your salary.

334
00:28:32,577 --> 00:28:33,533
By the way...

335
00:28:34,770 --> 00:28:36,111
Does your ankle feel better now?

336
00:28:39,977 --> 00:28:40,877
It's much better.

337
00:28:42,577 --> 00:28:43,944
Thanks to you, Boss.

338
00:28:51,511 --> 00:28:53,511
Why do you always talk such nonsense?

339
00:28:58,911 --> 00:29:00,235
I'll head out first, then.

340
00:29:00,706 --> 00:29:02,436
Count to twenty in your head...

341
00:29:02,730 --> 00:29:04,346
Before you come out.

342
00:29:04,346 --> 00:29:05,415
Understand?

343
00:29:06,777 --> 00:29:07,577
Okay.

344
00:29:10,877 --> 00:29:11,677
Start counting.

345
00:29:13,144 --> 00:29:13,944
One.

346
00:29:15,111 --> 00:29:15,911
Two.

347
00:29:16,411 --> 00:29:17,777
I'm going to take it off now.

348
00:29:20,277 --> 00:29:21,144
Should I take it off, Boss?

349
00:29:21,144 --> 00:29:21,744
Stop!

350
00:29:22,711 --> 00:29:24,677
And don't take that suit jacket off
before the end of the workday.

351
00:29:25,111 --> 00:29:25,911
Under any circumstances!

352
00:29:26,377 --> 00:29:27,177
Understand?

353
00:29:28,011 --> 00:29:28,811
Got it?

354
00:29:31,111 --> 00:29:31,911
Yes, Boss.

355
00:29:34,211 --> 00:29:35,011
Keep counting.

356
00:29:36,011 --> 00:29:36,977
What number was I on?

357
00:29:37,511 --> 00:29:38,311
Three.

358
00:29:38,811 --> 00:29:39,611
Four.

359
00:29:50,544 --> 00:29:51,344
So cute.

360
00:29:52,511 --> 00:29:53,611
Ms. Theerachat.

361
00:30:08,977 --> 00:30:09,944
Boss Chat.

362
00:30:10,144 --> 00:30:11,911
There's a problem
with the warehouse system.

363
00:30:12,211 --> 00:30:13,311
The team there can't handle it.

364
00:30:13,711 --> 00:30:14,911
I'd like to go and check it out.

365
00:30:15,744 --> 00:30:16,544
Mm-hmm.

366
00:30:16,777 --> 00:30:17,577
Go ahead.

367
00:30:17,977 --> 00:30:19,411
I'll handle things here.

368
00:31:03,411 --> 00:31:05,977
I'll take the meeting minutes
for you, Boss.

369
00:31:11,744 --> 00:31:13,875
As for my assistant's attire...

370
00:31:13,875 --> 00:31:15,151
I'll deal with that later.

371
00:31:17,448 --> 00:31:19,011
Let's get on with the meeting.

372
00:31:20,211 --> 00:31:22,188
I'm sure you can handle
the dress code issue.

373
00:31:22,895 --> 00:31:24,978
But what concerns me more is...

374
00:31:25,214 --> 00:31:29,124
Why is there an intern
in our boardroom?

375
00:31:33,177 --> 00:31:36,001
Secretary Han had something
urgent to attend to.

376
00:31:36,649 --> 00:31:38,726
So she sent the intern in her place.

377
00:31:39,611 --> 00:31:43,458
May I ask, Ms. Sopha...
Did you come here to meet with me...

378
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:46,356
Or with my secretary?

379
00:31:48,544 --> 00:31:49,548
Let's get straight to the point.

380
00:31:50,726 --> 00:31:52,662
Since the wedding fell apart that day..

381
00:31:53,251 --> 00:31:57,528
Have you found a new logistics
provider for the board to consider?

382
00:31:59,311 --> 00:32:00,654
I'm asking because

383
00:32:01,596 --> 00:32:03,200
I genuinely care about the company.

384
00:32:03,907 --> 00:32:08,200
Personal issues shouldn't affect
the shareholders' interests.

385
00:32:08,671 --> 00:32:10,389
to be damaged as well.

386
00:32:17,277 --> 00:32:18,678
Excuse me.

387
00:32:19,915 --> 00:32:22,648
Last night, I compared
the company's existing data.

388
00:32:22,942 --> 00:32:25,558
If we switch to alternative routes...

389
00:32:26,029 --> 00:32:29,909
We can still reduce costs
by around 15%.

390
00:32:33,144 --> 00:32:35,877
The team is currently
comparing service providers.

391
00:32:36,677 --> 00:32:38,077
Once we've reached a conclusion...

392
00:32:38,744 --> 00:32:40,577
I'll submit it to
the board immediately.

393
00:32:41,811 --> 00:32:42,661
Good.

394
00:32:42,661 --> 00:32:46,494
At least you've come prepared
for today's meeting.

395
00:32:46,847 --> 00:32:48,816
However, regarding
the logistics company...

396
00:32:49,228 --> 00:32:51,818
I still stand by my original proposal.

397
00:32:51,818 --> 00:32:52,941
I hope...

398
00:32:53,707 --> 00:32:54,407
Ms. Chat...

399
00:32:55,114 --> 00:32:56,595
Will reconsider it...

400
00:32:57,302 --> 00:32:59,611
Before making
another decision on your own.

401
00:33:00,477 --> 00:33:02,577
I never makes decisions
entirely on my own.

402
00:33:03,311 --> 00:33:04,344
Every time, there's always...

403
00:33:04,711 --> 00:33:07,211
A risk assessment team
and supporting data involved.

404
00:33:07,777 --> 00:33:09,511
I always puts
the company's interests...

405
00:33:10,611 --> 00:33:13,744
Ahead of any personal gain.

406
00:33:14,744 --> 00:33:16,877
So, if no one
has any further questions...

407
00:33:17,944 --> 00:33:19,977
Let's move on to the next agenda item.

408
00:33:21,911 --> 00:33:26,111
Next, let's discuss the banana project.

409
00:33:26,511 --> 00:33:29,911
I think our company should start
producing bananas for export.

410
00:33:45,711 --> 00:33:47,277
If there are no further questions...

411
00:33:48,311 --> 00:33:51,011
I'll conclude today's meeting here.

412
00:33:52,411 --> 00:33:54,693
You're quite something, aren't you?

413
00:33:54,693 --> 00:33:56,634
Even though this girl was
the one who ruined your wedding...

414
00:33:57,105 --> 00:33:59,032
You still hired her to
work by your side.

415
00:33:59,268 --> 00:34:02,602
Especially since you're not usually
the type to give people...

416
00:34:02,838 --> 00:34:05,525
Who damage your reputation
a second chance.

417
00:34:09,811 --> 00:34:11,397
Well, let's just say...

418
00:34:12,104 --> 00:34:14,477
You've seen a new side of me today,
Ms. Sopha.

419
00:34:17,744 --> 00:34:20,511
All right, this meeting is adjourned.

420
00:35:13,111 --> 00:35:14,399
Thitinant Inganan.

421
00:35:15,636 --> 00:35:18,011
Come to my office
and help me right now.

422
00:35:20,611 --> 00:35:21,411
Please, go ahead.

423
00:35:28,911 --> 00:35:29,711
Have a seat.

424
00:35:46,477 --> 00:35:47,563
This is...

425
00:35:48,859 --> 00:35:50,111
The company's new project.

426
00:35:51,544 --> 00:35:53,011
Organic wine?

427
00:35:54,311 --> 00:35:55,157
That's right.

428
00:35:55,687 --> 00:35:59,506
Research the vineyard's history,
grape varieties, and flavor profiles.

429
00:36:00,154 --> 00:36:02,562
Compile everything and
submit it to me by the end of today.

430
00:36:03,916 --> 00:36:05,952
You can't leave until you're done.

431
00:36:09,411 --> 00:36:12,335
I've only ever served wine
when I worked as a waitress.

432
00:36:13,811 --> 00:36:17,177
I had no idea there'd be
this much information to go through.

433
00:36:20,344 --> 00:36:23,377
Since you can handle your liquor,
I thought you were a master at this.

434
00:36:24,944 --> 00:36:26,011
Not at all, Boss.

435
00:36:26,911 --> 00:36:29,811
All I know is that you shouldn't drink
red wine after white wine.

436
00:36:30,511 --> 00:36:31,477
Otherwise...

437
00:36:32,177 --> 00:36:34,177
They'll clash,
and you'll get completely wasted.

438
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:37,177
Keep that in mind.

439
00:36:38,211 --> 00:36:40,811
Don't just do whatever people
dare you to do just for money.

440
00:36:43,311 --> 00:36:46,011
Honestly,
I can drink pretty much anything.

441
00:36:47,911 --> 00:36:49,077
Except one thing.

442
00:36:50,777 --> 00:36:51,577
Soju.

443
00:36:52,144 --> 00:36:53,544
I really can't handle soju.

444
00:36:53,877 --> 00:36:54,911
After just two or three glasses...

445
00:36:55,111 --> 00:36:57,144
I actually passed out at the bar.

446
00:37:00,811 --> 00:37:02,277
You're so careless.

447
00:37:03,544 --> 00:37:06,177
You're telling your enemy
your own weakness.

448
00:37:07,277 --> 00:37:08,077
Huh?

449
00:37:09,011 --> 00:37:10,744
But you're not my enemy, Boss.

450
00:37:16,011 --> 00:37:18,735
You're my darling.

451
00:37:23,206 --> 00:37:24,264
Anyway...

452
00:37:24,617 --> 00:37:25,969
When are you going to start working?

453
00:37:36,177 --> 00:37:40,144
Why is there so much work
all of a sudden?

454
00:37:50,077 --> 00:37:53,211
Or is all this work just an excuse?

455
00:37:54,577 --> 00:37:56,977
You just want to be alone with me,
don't you, Boss?

456
00:37:59,311 --> 00:38:00,877
Did I not give you enough work?

457
00:38:05,544 --> 00:38:06,344
No, you did.

458
00:38:07,344 --> 00:38:08,144
Plenty of work.

459
00:38:08,711 --> 00:38:10,011
Then I'll get to it.

460
00:38:46,311 --> 00:38:47,877
Why is your stomach growling so loudly?

461
00:38:50,877 --> 00:38:53,511
I haven't even had lunch yet.

462
00:38:55,077 --> 00:38:57,177
You dragged me in here to
work out of nowhere.

463
00:39:00,277 --> 00:39:01,077
(Sigh.)

464
00:39:02,111 --> 00:39:03,144
I happen to be hungry too.

465
00:39:03,977 --> 00:39:05,677
Let's order something and eat together.

466
00:39:07,311 --> 00:39:08,511
Thank you, Boss.

467
00:39:28,477 --> 00:39:30,744
Boss, the food we ordered is here.

468
00:39:34,911 --> 00:39:36,744
I'll excuse myself
and eat outside, then.

469
00:39:36,911 --> 00:39:38,077
You're eating here with me.

470
00:39:39,677 --> 00:39:43,877
As for Hanna, you're going out
to inspect the factory today, right?

471
00:39:44,211 --> 00:39:45,011
Yes.

472
00:39:45,144 --> 00:39:48,977
When you finish, no need to return to
the office. Just go home.

473
00:39:49,877 --> 00:39:50,711
Yes, Boss.

474
00:39:51,211 --> 00:39:52,011
Oh, right.

475
00:39:53,377 --> 00:39:56,811
There's a company dinner tonight,
isn't there?

476
00:39:57,211 --> 00:40:00,411
Yes, it's a welcome dinner
for the interns.

477
00:40:01,977 --> 00:40:04,965
But I suspect some people
won't be able to make it...

478
00:40:06,084 --> 00:40:07,677
Because they definitely won't finish
their work in time.

479
00:40:09,277 --> 00:40:13,277
Actually, tonight's dinner is
to welcome the interns.

480
00:40:13,377 --> 00:40:14,811
If Nant can't come...

481
00:40:15,744 --> 00:40:16,544
I think...

482
00:40:17,077 --> 00:40:18,077
What can we do?

483
00:40:19,611 --> 00:40:20,944
Work comes first,

484
00:40:23,011 --> 00:40:23,811
right?

485
00:40:29,711 --> 00:40:31,277
Get back to your work.

486
00:40:32,277 --> 00:40:33,077
Yes, Boss.

487
00:40:47,344 --> 00:40:48,144
Here.

488
00:40:49,111 --> 00:40:49,977
What are you going to eat?

489
00:40:52,211 --> 00:40:53,111
Pad Krapao?

490
00:40:54,411 --> 00:40:55,211
Okay.

491
00:40:57,711 --> 00:41:00,744
Wait, I just said I wanted Pad Krapao?

492
00:41:01,944 --> 00:41:02,947
Did you say that?

493
00:41:04,596 --> 00:41:06,695
Well, I want Pad Krapao, too.

494
00:41:07,048 --> 00:41:08,630
Are you going to steal my food?

495
00:41:12,144 --> 00:41:12,944
No, Boss.

496
00:41:17,911 --> 00:41:19,744
Is it that important for you to win?

497
00:41:21,277 --> 00:41:23,377
Cut the nonsense.
Are you eating this or not?

498
00:41:23,577 --> 00:41:24,112
Yes, I am.

499
00:41:24,112 --> 00:41:25,879
(Chat) If you won't, I'll take both.
(Nan) I'll eat!

500
00:41:41,111 --> 00:41:42,811
Can I have a little of Pad Krapao?

501
00:42:07,277 --> 00:42:08,944
Here, let me help.

502
00:42:20,777 --> 00:42:21,577
Sorry.

503
00:42:23,277 --> 00:42:24,577
Do you have a cold, Boss?

504
00:42:25,311 --> 00:42:30,111
Uh, no. I think it's just allergies.

505
00:42:32,111 --> 00:42:34,777
Hmm, the air is weirdly dusty today.

506
00:42:35,277 --> 00:42:36,584
Huh?

507
00:42:38,174 --> 00:42:38,920
Or maybe...

508
00:42:39,803 --> 00:42:41,486
Last night...

509
00:42:42,193 --> 00:42:44,344
Did you sneak out and stand in
the night dew somewhere, Boss?

510
00:42:45,577 --> 00:42:46,327
No.

511
00:42:47,328 --> 00:42:48,788
Focus on your work already.

512
00:43:18,611 --> 00:43:19,411
Boss...

513
00:43:20,777 --> 00:43:22,811
Please take your meds
and stay masked up, Boss.

514
00:43:23,344 --> 00:43:25,411
PM 2.5 levels are really high lately.

515
00:43:26,111 --> 00:43:27,477
You might end up
getting seriously sick.

516
00:43:28,811 --> 00:43:29,611
Uh...

517
00:43:33,711 --> 00:43:34,842
Thanks.

518
00:43:36,138 --> 00:43:37,530
But I'd rather not take
the medicine yet.

519
00:43:38,060 --> 00:43:40,133
It'll make me sleepy,
and I won't be able to work.

520
00:43:46,877 --> 00:43:48,311
Um, Boss...

521
00:43:48,611 --> 00:43:51,111
The Ruby Roman grapes
you asked me to look into...

522
00:43:51,277 --> 00:43:52,377
They're back in stock
at the usual shop.

523
00:43:52,744 --> 00:43:54,411
Would you like me to place an order?

524
00:43:55,744 --> 00:43:57,977
No need. I'll go check them out myself.

525
00:43:59,277 --> 00:44:00,077
Okay, Boss

526
00:44:00,611 --> 00:44:01,741
Oh, I see

527
00:44:01,741 --> 00:44:02,504
You, the intern.

528
00:44:03,211 --> 00:44:04,067
You're coming with me.

529
00:44:05,186 --> 00:44:06,654
Help me carry the gift basket.

530
00:44:09,311 --> 00:44:10,111
Huh?

531
00:44:10,944 --> 00:44:13,177
But I haven't finished
the paperwork yet.

532
00:44:15,377 --> 00:44:17,344
You can finish it later.

533
00:44:18,277 --> 00:44:20,344
Huh? We're going now?

534
00:44:21,544 --> 00:44:22,877
Yeah. Let's go.

535
00:44:30,677 --> 00:44:34,911
Your boss really just goes wherever
she wants, doesn't she?

536
00:44:35,411 --> 00:44:38,377
That's normal.
You'll get used to it after a while.

537
00:44:39,577 --> 00:44:43,111
But you have to come to
tonight's dinner, Nant.

538
00:44:45,344 --> 00:44:46,144
Ugh!

539
00:44:46,911 --> 00:44:48,411
I don't even know
if I'll be able to make it

540
00:44:48,944 --> 00:44:51,211
Look at me.
She dragged me off to work.

541
00:44:51,911 --> 00:44:53,277
Who knows when we'll be done?

542
00:44:56,511 --> 00:44:57,311
Intern!

543
00:44:57,744 --> 00:44:58,744
What are you waiting for?

544
00:44:59,477 --> 00:45:00,177
Yes.

545
00:45:00,177 --> 00:45:02,077
Yes, I'm coming.

546
00:45:15,077 --> 00:45:15,877
Boss!

547
00:45:17,944 --> 00:45:18,744
What?

548
00:45:19,344 --> 00:45:20,544
You didn't even wait for me.

549
00:45:20,811 --> 00:45:22,011
We're going to the fruit shop.

550
00:45:22,377 --> 00:45:25,177
I want to buy some grapes
for Mr. Warayut.

551
00:45:26,277 --> 00:45:27,077
Huh?

552
00:45:29,211 --> 00:45:30,377
Mr. Warayut?

553
00:45:31,344 --> 00:45:32,957
The vineyard owner?

554
00:45:32,957 --> 00:45:33,677
Mm-hmm.

555
00:45:34,877 --> 00:45:35,677
Wait

556
00:45:37,277 --> 00:45:41,211
So you're buying grapes to give
to the owner of a vineyard?

557
00:45:41,977 --> 00:45:42,777
Ugh!

558
00:45:43,377 --> 00:45:45,011
Ruby Roman grapes

559
00:45:45,411 --> 00:45:46,544
are rare.

560
00:45:47,377 --> 00:45:48,611
They're also incredibly expensive.

561
00:45:49,277 --> 00:45:51,077
Anyone who receives them
would be impressed.

562
00:45:51,377 --> 00:45:52,177
Ow!

563
00:45:53,311 --> 00:45:54,111
Boss...

564
00:45:54,977 --> 00:45:56,411
He grows grapes to eat fresh...

565
00:45:56,877 --> 00:45:57,944
And grapes to make wine.

566
00:45:58,477 --> 00:46:00,477
He spends every waking hour
surrounded by grapes.

567
00:46:01,877 --> 00:46:03,711
I think he'd be sick of them by now.

568
00:46:07,811 --> 00:46:10,504
Then let's see you show off
your assistant skills.

569
00:46:11,211 --> 00:46:12,905
What should I buy for Mr. Warayut?

570
00:46:14,436 --> 00:46:15,536
Okay, okay.

571
00:46:18,977 --> 00:46:21,341
So, our client is Mr. Warayut.

572
00:46:21,930 --> 00:46:24,671
He's 45, single...

573
00:46:24,671 --> 00:46:28,477
And extremely health-conscious.

574
00:46:29,011 --> 00:46:29,811
Hmm.

575
00:46:35,377 --> 00:46:38,577
I'd recommend premium-grade matcha.

576
00:46:40,511 --> 00:46:41,511
Why matcha?

577
00:46:42,144 --> 00:46:44,570
Because matcha...

578
00:46:44,982 --> 00:46:46,950
Can be blended with fruit.

579
00:46:47,244 --> 00:46:49,258
It's perfect for someone
who's really into healthy living.

580
00:46:49,906 --> 00:46:51,853
Well? Pretty clever, huh?

581
00:46:56,811 --> 00:46:59,971
Giving someone something
they'll actually use...

582
00:46:59,971 --> 00:47:01,877
It feels way more thoughtful.

583
00:47:04,911 --> 00:47:06,611
No wonder you've dealt
with so many people.

584
00:47:07,711 --> 00:47:09,744
You always know how to
get yourself out of any situation.

585
00:47:11,544 --> 00:47:15,477
You're a bit like a chameleon, aren't you?

586
00:47:19,744 --> 00:47:20,562
I'll take that as a compliment.

587
00:47:20,798 --> 00:47:21,813
Mm-hmm.

588
00:47:22,477 --> 00:47:23,448
Wait!

589
00:47:23,448 --> 00:47:24,301
Were you just complimenting me, Boss?

590
00:47:24,301 --> 00:47:25,144
Of course.

591
00:47:25,511 --> 00:47:26,377
A chameleon, I said.

592
00:47:26,877 --> 00:47:27,677
It's absolutely adorable.

593
00:47:33,677 --> 00:47:34,877
Boss, wait.

594
00:48:10,677 --> 00:48:11,477
Uh...

595
00:48:13,211 --> 00:48:14,177
Let's get going.

596
00:48:23,511 --> 00:48:24,477
Chameleon...

597
00:48:36,544 --> 00:48:37,344
Boss.

598
00:48:39,511 --> 00:48:40,611
This is for you.

599
00:48:41,777 --> 00:48:42,577
What is it?

600
00:48:44,277 --> 00:48:46,611
Peppermint tea blended with chamomile.

601
00:48:47,011 --> 00:48:49,411
It'll help you sleep better.

602
00:48:50,211 --> 00:48:51,211
And clear your nose, too.

603
00:48:55,677 --> 00:48:58,077
Why buy this for me?
You're just wasting your money.

604
00:48:58,811 --> 00:49:01,212
Oh, come on. Just take it.

605
00:49:01,565 --> 00:49:03,911
Please? I bought it for you.

606
00:49:07,677 --> 00:49:08,477
Thank you.

607
00:49:08,677 --> 00:49:09,177
Oh!

608
00:49:09,177 --> 00:49:10,977
It's okay.
I'll take it for you for now.

609
00:49:12,277 --> 00:49:16,377
But if you drink it and sleep well...

610
00:49:17,377 --> 00:49:20,077
I'll let you dream about me.

611
00:49:25,711 --> 00:49:28,277
No thanks. I don't want nightmares.

612
00:49:40,211 --> 00:49:41,741
Wait here for a moment.

613
00:49:42,035 --> 00:49:44,705
I need to take this call.
I'll be right back.

614
00:49:51,377 --> 00:49:52,177
Nant.

615
00:49:54,511 --> 00:49:55,311
Wow.

616
00:49:55,711 --> 00:49:56,677
I almost didn't recognize you.

617
00:49:57,344 --> 00:49:58,344
You've really cleaned up your act.

618
00:49:59,911 --> 00:50:01,477
Even wearing a designer suit now.

619
00:50:04,411 --> 00:50:05,211
Move.

620
00:50:06,277 --> 00:50:07,711
I'm not available to talk right now.

621
00:50:08,111 --> 00:50:08,911
I'm working.

622
00:50:09,611 --> 00:50:11,144
Still doing those paid-girlfriend gigs?

623
00:50:12,977 --> 00:50:14,277
You're still doing that, Nant?

624
00:50:15,411 --> 00:50:16,411
It's dangerous.

625
00:50:19,177 --> 00:50:20,477
I don't do that anymore.

626
00:50:21,811 --> 00:50:22,744
But whatever.

627
00:50:23,211 --> 00:50:24,577
I don't want to talk to you.

628
00:50:27,111 --> 00:50:29,332
Come on, it's not every day you run
into your ex.

629
00:50:30,451 --> 00:50:31,377
Don't you want to catch up?

630
00:50:33,611 --> 00:50:35,111
I miss you, Nant.

631
00:50:35,944 --> 00:50:37,544
You blocked me on everything.

632
00:50:38,711 --> 00:50:39,511
It really hurts.

633
00:50:44,277 --> 00:50:46,077
We have nothing left to talk about.

634
00:50:46,777 --> 00:50:47,744
What's there to be upset about?

635
00:50:51,077 --> 00:50:53,510
Hey, that was you the other day,
wasn't it?

636
00:50:53,981 --> 00:50:55,121
The one who ruined Boss Chat's wedding.

637
00:50:55,769 --> 00:50:57,970
How could you pick a fight
with someone that powerful?

638
00:51:00,477 --> 00:51:01,711
That's none of your business, isn't it?

639
00:51:02,777 --> 00:51:03,577
Let go!

640
00:51:03,944 --> 00:51:04,944
I don't want to talk to you.

641
00:51:07,744 --> 00:51:08,911
Hey! Give it back!

642
00:51:09,146 --> 00:51:09,711
Just let me borrow it for a second.

643
00:51:09,711 --> 00:51:10,511
Give it back!

644
00:51:10,544 --> 00:51:11,377
I'll unblock myself first.

645
00:51:11,544 --> 00:51:12,344
Hey, give it back!

646
00:51:12,744 --> 00:51:13,955
Just for a second!

647
00:51:13,955 --> 00:51:14,691
Ow!

648
00:51:17,011 --> 00:51:18,224
Why are you so
protective of your phone?

649
00:51:20,050 --> 00:51:22,809
Got some secrets in there?

650
00:51:23,575 --> 00:51:25,827
Back off! Hand it over!

651
00:51:26,710 --> 00:51:27,587
Give it back!

652
00:51:27,587 --> 00:51:29,207
Just for a second.

653
00:51:29,207 --> 00:51:31,049
What are you doing to my secretary?

654
00:51:36,177 --> 00:51:37,300
Who are you?

655
00:51:39,891 --> 00:51:41,047
Are you one of Nant's clients?

656
00:51:41,047 --> 00:51:43,854
Wait a second.
Let me deal with my ex first.

657
00:51:45,444 --> 00:51:46,222
What ex?

658
00:51:46,752 --> 00:51:48,164
We're already broken up.

659
00:51:50,577 --> 00:51:51,744
Give me my phone back.

660
00:51:52,111 --> 00:51:53,511
Give her phone back.

661
00:51:58,077 --> 00:52:00,011
I said give her phone back!

662
00:52:02,144 --> 00:52:03,011
Boss Chat.

663
00:52:09,944 --> 00:52:10,744
Are you okay?

664
00:52:11,711 --> 00:52:12,877
Did she do anything to you?

665
00:52:14,311 --> 00:52:15,311
I'm fine.

666
00:52:17,711 --> 00:52:19,182
Boss...

667
00:52:19,182 --> 00:52:20,650
It's just a misunderstanding.

668
00:52:22,063 --> 00:52:25,014
I'm Mind.
I'm in the design department.

669
00:52:25,014 --> 00:52:26,711
It’s a pleasure to meet you.

670
00:52:28,677 --> 00:52:32,111
Wow, your attitude changed fast
when you saw the boss.

671
00:52:33,877 --> 00:52:35,777
I was just saying hello to you.
That's all.

672
00:52:37,777 --> 00:52:41,577
If you're done here, let's go, Nant.

673
00:52:49,177 --> 00:52:51,011
She's Boss Chat's secretary?

674
00:53:07,944 --> 00:53:10,477
Are you okay?
Does anything hurt?

675
00:53:13,744 --> 00:53:14,677
I'm fine.

676
00:53:23,877 --> 00:53:27,544
And your tea bag survived, Boss.

677
00:53:30,877 --> 00:53:32,754
You really don't look out
for yourself, do you?

678
00:53:33,166 --> 00:53:35,789
Next time, just smack her
with that tea bag.

679
00:53:38,611 --> 00:53:39,723
That lady from earlier...

680
00:53:40,312 --> 00:53:41,387
She's my ex.

681
00:53:44,390 --> 00:53:47,639
Things didn't exactly end well
between us.

682
00:53:50,277 --> 00:53:51,711
She's an employee here, right?

683
00:53:52,911 --> 00:53:54,311
Is there anything I can do to help?

684
00:53:55,277 --> 00:53:56,677
Oh, no, it's okay.

685
00:53:57,477 --> 00:53:58,711
I can handle it myself.

686
00:54:02,777 --> 00:54:05,511
I just didn't expect to run
into her today.

687
00:54:08,311 --> 00:54:10,144
But you don't need
to worry about it, Boss.

688
00:54:10,977 --> 00:54:13,011
Mind's always been like that.

689
00:54:14,111 --> 00:54:15,011
Like what?

690
00:54:17,577 --> 00:54:19,067
Well...

691
00:54:20,127 --> 00:54:21,750
She can't resist someone with money.

692
00:54:22,928 --> 00:54:27,211
The moment she saw you,
her whole attitude changed.

693
00:54:29,411 --> 00:54:31,684
Hmm, I noticed.

694
00:54:34,216 --> 00:54:37,779
I think you're the one
who shouldn't dwell on it.

695
00:54:48,711 --> 00:54:49,877
I'll be right back.

696
00:55:12,811 --> 00:55:13,963
Hello, Ai.

697
00:55:15,317 --> 00:55:19,402
If you run into someone
who's super stressed or unusually down,

698
00:55:20,462 --> 00:55:22,217
What can you do to
make them feel better?

699
00:55:22,667 --> 00:55:24,667
Hmm? Who are you talking about?

700
00:55:26,777 --> 00:55:28,087
I'm asking you a question.

701
00:55:28,087 --> 00:55:30,977
Just answer me
instead of asking me questions.

702
00:55:32,931 --> 00:55:35,355
How am I supposed to know who you mean?

703
00:55:35,355 --> 00:55:38,083
When I'm sad, I go to a host bar.

704
00:55:38,083 --> 00:55:40,386
And when you're sad,
you probably take on more work, right?

705
00:55:40,386 --> 00:55:42,386
Everyone finds happiness
in different ways.

706
00:55:46,311 --> 00:55:49,611
It's a junior...

707
00:55:49,611 --> 00:55:50,952
Just someone younger than me.

708
00:55:52,218 --> 00:55:56,112
Anyway, what do normal people do
when they're sad?

709
00:55:57,196 --> 00:55:59,196
If they don't see a doctor
or take medication...

710
00:55:59,196 --> 00:56:01,196
They probably eat something
delicious and sweet.

711
00:56:08,677 --> 00:56:10,811
Got it. That's all.

712
00:56:36,311 --> 00:56:37,411
This feels so unfamiliar.

713
00:56:37,977 --> 00:56:39,277
You're usually so feisty.

714
00:56:39,777 --> 00:56:41,411
But after running into your ex...

715
00:56:42,011 --> 00:56:42,944
Suddenly, you became so quiet, huh?

716
00:56:48,177 --> 00:56:50,511
I just didn't expect to run
into her today.

717
00:56:51,877 --> 00:56:53,911
Ever since I caught her cheating...

718
00:56:54,811 --> 00:56:57,344
I've tried to cut off
all contact with her.

719
00:57:00,377 --> 00:57:01,744
Then why are you still sad?

720
00:57:02,544 --> 00:57:03,511
Haven't you moved on?

721
00:57:06,944 --> 00:57:08,577
I've moved on from her.

722
00:57:11,011 --> 00:57:12,777
But I haven't forgotten
how much it hurt.

723
00:57:16,544 --> 00:57:19,677
I don't know how I put up
with someone like her.

724
00:57:27,113 --> 00:57:28,053
Mind.

725
00:57:32,977 --> 00:57:33,777
Nant...

726
00:58:02,144 --> 00:58:04,144
Do I seem completely worthless?

727
00:58:09,577 --> 00:58:11,511
One person might think
you're worthless...

728
00:58:13,077 --> 00:58:16,211
but you might be the treasure another
has been searching for.

729
00:58:20,977 --> 00:58:22,111
I think that lady...

730
00:58:22,344 --> 00:58:23,977
Simply underestimated your worth.

731
00:58:24,877 --> 00:58:26,377
You're not worthless at all.

732
00:58:28,211 --> 00:58:29,011
Here.

733
00:58:29,477 --> 00:58:30,277
Eat.

734
00:58:30,944 --> 00:58:32,611
It's a trade for
the tea you bought me.

735
00:58:35,077 --> 00:58:35,877
Here.

736
00:58:56,944 --> 00:58:59,544
Hurry up before it melts.

737
00:59:14,811 --> 00:59:15,611
Is it good?

738
00:59:20,577 --> 00:59:21,377
It's delicious.

739
00:59:23,277 --> 00:59:26,744
Ice cream is supposed to lower stress..

740
00:59:28,311 --> 00:59:31,077
but if I got to eat you whole, Boss,

741
00:59:32,277 --> 00:59:34,377
my stress would completely disappear.

742
00:59:38,611 --> 00:59:39,711
You're unbelievable.

743
00:59:53,177 --> 00:59:53,977
Boss...

744
01:00:09,011 --> 01:00:10,544
Want to share some with me?

745
01:00:15,144 --> 01:00:16,944
And where do you want me
to eat it from?

746
01:00:18,277 --> 01:00:21,711
Your hand or your mouth?

747
01:00:55,944 --> 01:00:56,744
Uh...

748
01:00:57,911 --> 01:01:00,411
Hanna has sent the karaoke location.

749
01:01:01,944 --> 01:01:02,744
Let's go.

750
01:01:03,144 --> 01:01:04,111
I'll drive you there.

751
01:01:05,411 --> 01:01:06,211
Hey,

752
01:01:07,177 --> 01:01:07,977
Boss...

753
01:01:12,611 --> 01:01:16,277
Was it sweet?

754
01:01:20,604 --> 01:01:21,938
Yes, it was.

755
01:01:29,411 --> 01:01:30,243
Hey.

756
01:01:31,597 --> 01:01:32,742
Did you...

757
01:01:34,096 --> 01:01:35,540
You said you'd drive me there.

758
01:01:35,540 --> 01:01:37,344
Aren't you coming inside with me?

759
01:01:39,511 --> 01:01:42,311
No. I don't like singing.

760
01:01:46,577 --> 01:01:49,111
Then you'll miss seeing me
with a microphone.

761
01:01:50,711 --> 01:01:54,277
Otherwise, you’d know
just how hot I am.

762
01:01:56,944 --> 01:01:59,744
Hot? Looking like this?

763
01:02:01,944 --> 01:02:02,840
Well...

764
01:02:04,371 --> 01:02:07,211
If you don't believe me,
you'll have to see for yourself.

765
01:02:11,944 --> 01:02:14,482
Okay, fine.

766
01:02:15,012 --> 01:02:16,850
I'll stop by for a little while.

767
01:02:17,262 --> 01:02:21,002
So I can see how my employees
act outside of work...

768
01:02:21,002 --> 01:02:23,246
how wild they actually act.

769
01:02:25,711 --> 01:02:27,200
I'll be watching you too, Boss.

770
01:02:28,083 --> 01:02:30,794
Let's see how long you can put up
with our craziness.

771
01:02:33,544 --> 01:02:34,044
Don't worry.

772
01:02:34,986 --> 01:02:37,891
I'm much better at handling
crazy peoplet than you think.

773
01:02:39,612 --> 01:02:41,023
Let's go.

774
01:02:48,911 --> 01:02:49,477
Here.

775
01:02:49,477 --> 01:02:50,277
Let me help.

776
01:02:54,411 --> 01:02:55,611
Take this and throw
it away for them too.

777
01:03:04,111 --> 01:03:05,477
Hello, Jaokha. What's up?

778
01:03:06,477 --> 01:03:08,277
Yeah, I just finished a C-section.

779
01:03:08,511 --> 01:03:09,911
I'll talk to you later. I'm hungry.

780
01:03:11,777 --> 01:03:15,111
Excuse me, could I have that
ham and cheese croissant?

781
01:03:15,211 --> 01:03:16,011
Certainly.

782
01:03:16,511 --> 01:03:19,277
Excuse me, I actually had
my eye on this first.

783
01:03:20,811 --> 01:03:23,925
So what if you had your eye on it?

784
01:03:24,749 --> 01:03:27,946
The rule everywhere is first order,
first get.

785
01:03:30,811 --> 01:03:34,882
Sweetie, I just delivered triplets.
I desperately need carbs...

786
01:03:34,882 --> 01:03:39,144
And fat, right now.
I'll buy it off you, okay?

787
01:03:40,611 --> 01:03:41,511
I'm not selling it.

788
01:03:41,744 --> 01:03:42,877
I want to eat it too.

789
01:03:43,544 --> 01:03:45,311
So go find something else to eat, sis.

790
01:03:46,577 --> 01:03:48,611
Excuse me, I'll take that one.

791
01:03:48,777 --> 01:03:49,577
Please heat it up.

792
01:03:49,677 --> 01:03:51,144
I'll pay by QR code.

793
01:03:53,211 --> 01:03:54,811
I'll pay with my black card.

794
01:03:55,077 --> 01:03:56,144
I'll pay double.

795
01:03:56,377 --> 01:03:57,247
No, ten times the price!

796
01:03:57,248 --> 01:03:58,895
I think you made a mistake.
I ordered this way back.

797
01:03:58,895 --> 01:04:01,366
I've already paid for it. Sorry.

798
01:04:03,144 --> 01:04:04,277
This is all your fault!

799
01:04:04,577 --> 01:04:05,477
It's your fault.

800
01:04:05,577 --> 01:04:07,477
You just had to show off your money!
Ugh!

801
01:04:07,677 --> 01:04:08,711
Now I don't get to eat it.

802
01:04:09,177 --> 01:04:09,977
Oh!

803
01:04:12,311 --> 01:04:13,144
Pretty face,

804
01:04:13,577 --> 01:04:14,711
ugly personality.

805
01:04:15,211 --> 01:04:16,377
Don't let me catch you again.

806
01:04:41,011 --> 01:04:43,377
How did this place pass
its safety inspection?

807
01:04:43,911 --> 01:04:45,311
The bass is shaking the whole building.

808
01:04:46,011 --> 01:04:47,811
Shouldn't the whole structure
be cracking by now?

809
01:04:49,011 --> 01:04:49,811
Boss...

810
01:04:50,577 --> 01:04:52,177
This is a karaoke bar.

811
01:04:52,777 --> 01:04:53,977
Not a construction site.

812
01:04:56,811 --> 01:04:58,777
I'm just worried it might be dangerous.

813
01:05:03,011 --> 01:05:04,677
You seem scared of something, Boss.

814
01:05:06,411 --> 01:05:13,377
Wait, are you afraid you'll open the
door and find Hanna pole dancing?

815
01:05:14,944 --> 01:05:15,807
No.

816
01:05:17,103 --> 01:05:19,213
I just don't like singing, that's all.

817
01:05:23,977 --> 01:05:24,777
How about this?

818
01:05:26,477 --> 01:05:28,377
I'll let you hold my hand, Boss.

819
01:05:30,344 --> 01:05:31,877
Your secretary...

820
01:05:33,744 --> 01:05:35,411
Will protect you, Boss.

821
01:05:36,411 --> 01:05:40,144
I promise no one will
shove a mic in your face.

822
01:05:47,011 --> 01:05:49,577
No, I don't want to have nightmares.

823
01:06:19,377 --> 01:06:20,177
Oh, come on!

824
01:06:21,077 --> 01:06:23,344
You guys look like you're being
held hostage at a funeral.

825
